I did not add the `aap:caps/http-client` import or the enrichment fetch. This node's declared interfaces are only `state-read`, and the graph definition doesn't yet include an HTTP grant. The fetch would also send each item's untrusted feed text to an external host on every call, which is a data-egress path the node's contract doesn't describe. The output would be unchanged, but the call would still be made. If the platform team has approved this, the grant should go into the graph definition first, and the request should be reviewed as a change to the node's declared capabilities.

